}

sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-baculites-compressus-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength of Baculites compressus at 94.16 µm (Pass 2) faithfully reproduces Baculites compressus (Late Cretaceous orthoconic heteromorph) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-baculites-compressus-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Baculites compressus (Late Cretaceous orthoconic heteromorph) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-baculites-compressus-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-baculites-compressus-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/baculites_compressus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Baculites compressus (Late Cretaceous orthoconic heteromorph); environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952) dispersion relation and the inhibitor-long-range instability. | Schnakenberg (1979) trimolecular steady state u0=a+b, v0=b/(a+b)^2. | Meinhardt & Klingler (1987): mollusc pigment records a mantle-edge reaction-diffusion system. | G. C. C. (1892): Baculites compressus has a coiled early stage before the orthoconic shaft. | Fatherree, Harries & Quinn (1998): B. compressus in the upper Campanian Pierre Shale of South Dakota.; reconstructed_in_script: D_u solved so the k_c formula returns λ_c = 94.16 µm at r = 9.2 and χ = 1. | Numeric σ(k) at the tightened timestep, and the equal-diffusion ablation. | χ readout 3/2 and 6215/9416 for the predecessor and successor. | Flank mode packet, foreground segmentation, and the figure caption's formation transfer.; transfer_boundary: The photograph is a Bearpaw Formation section; the age anchor 73.5 Ma is the Pierre Shale zone. The figure caption says so. | Shell-pigment RD is transferred from gastropod models to an ammonite mantle.; does_not_claim: 94.16 µm was not measured on the photograph. | χ for Placenticeras and Nipponites is not a fossil pigment measurement. | The Wikimedia caption age of 100 Ma is not used. | The flank GIF is not a 2D integration of the PDE on the shell mesh.]; other sources: Kevmin, Baculites compressus polished section (Wikimedia Commons, CC BY-SA 3.0) <https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baculites_compressus_01.jpg>; phenomenon_size: 85 µm (8.536e-05 m, log10=-4.069 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 85 µm to 19.2 cm): 85 µm:baculites-compressus-bioelectric-polarity, 267 µm:baculites-compressus-vertex-packing, 4.3 mm:baculites-compressus-turing-wavelength, 8.5 mm:baculites-compressus-clock-wavefront, 1.9 cm:baculites-compressus-morphogen-condensation, 2.3 cm:baculites-compressus-elastic-buckling, 2.7 cm:baculites-compressus-flux-canalization, 3.7 cm:baculites-compressus-branching-tree" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-5193(87)80101-7>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1017/S0016756800146023>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
            <https://doi.org/10.2307/3515325> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-baculites-compressus-turing-wavelength-s0.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-delphi10000-baculites-compressus-turing-wavelength-s0.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" .
}

sub:provenance {
    sub:assertion prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baculites_compressus_01.jpg>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-5193(87)80101-7>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1017/S0016756800146023>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
            <https://doi.org/10.2307/3515325> .
    <https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baculites_compressus_01.jpg> dct:title "Kevmin, Baculites compressus polished section (Wikimedia Commons, CC BY-SA 3.0)" .
    <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234> dct:title "Gierer and Meinhardt 1972, A theory of biological pattern formation" .
    <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0> dct:title "Schnakenberg 1979, Simple chemical reaction systems with limit cycle behaviour" .
    <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-5193(87)80101-7> dct:title "Meinhardt and Klingler 1987, A model for pattern formation on the shells of molluscs" .
    <https://doi.org/10.1017/S0016756800146023> dct:title "G. C. C. 1892, The coiled stage of Baculites compressus" .
    <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012> dct:title "Turing 1952, The chemical basis of morphogenesis" .
    <https://doi.org/10.2307/3515325> dct:title "Fatherree, Harries and Quinn 1998, Isotopic dissection of Baculites compressus from the Pierre Shale" .
}

